From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Martin=20=C5=A0trobl?= <recordyletsplays@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:51:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] ANDROID: nfc: s3fwrn5: Add a raw NCI character device

Android's NFC stack (libnfc-nci) is an NCI host in userspace: its HAL
needs the NCI packets of the chip, and features like host card emulation
only exist there. The kernel's NCI core does not hand packets out.

Add CONFIG_NFC_S3FWRN5_RAW. With it the chip is not registered with the
NCI core; /dev/s3fwrn5 carries its NCI packets instead (one packet per
read() and write(), one opener). The driver keeps the bus framing, the
interrupt, the power sequence and the clock. An ioctl switches the chip
off or power cycles it into NCI mode, and closing the device switches it
off. The bootloader mode is not reachable, so userspace cannot download
firmware.

Enable it in a3y17lte_defconfig for the NFC HAL of the Galaxy A3 (2017).
---
 arch/arm64/configs/a3y17lte_defconfig |   1 +
 drivers/nfc/s3fwrn5/Kconfig           |  11 ++
 drivers/nfc/s3fwrn5/Makefile          |   1 +
 drivers/nfc/s3fwrn5/core.c            |  14 +-
 drivers/nfc/s3fwrn5/raw.c             | 223 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/nfc/s3fwrn5/s3fwrn5.h         |   9 ++
 include/uapi/linux/s3fwrn5-raw.h      |  17 ++
 7 files changed, 274 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/nfc/s3fwrn5/raw.c
 create mode 100644 include/uapi/linux/s3fwrn5-raw.h

